# Where the Rainbow Six Siege catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-09-23**. `catalog.json` in this folder is the
list, in the two-kind form (`kinds`: Operators and Guns, see `../README.md`);
this file says where every fact and every picture in it came from.

**Pictures: publisher artwork only (decision D116).** Every picture in
`operators/` and `weapons/` is Ubisoft's own image, downloaded from Ubisoft's
image server staticctf.ubisoft.com, which is where Ubisoft's official Siege site
(ubisoft.com) serves it on that operator's page. None came from a fan wiki,
Fandom, an esports site or an image search. They are Ubisoft's copyright (Solid
Snake's icon is also Konami's: the operator pages carry a Konami copyright
notice for him), used in the app
to identify the operator or the gun, the same risk the owner accepted for the
game pictures in D116. Delete a `.png` and set that item's `image` to `null` and
the app shows its placeholder instead; nothing else changes.

- **`operators/`: the operator's official icon**, the square badge the game shows
  on its operator select screen and in the HUD, exactly as Ubisoft serves it on
  the operator's page (files named `r6s-operators-badge-<name>.png` or
  `Y<year>S<season>_BADGE_<Name>_L.png`), copied byte for byte: 201 x 201 for
  58 operators, 104 x 104 for the 20 whose page was made or remade recently.
  Transparent outside the badge. The operator portraits on the same pages (the
  tall character pictures) were **not** taken: the format has one picture per
  item, and the icon is what the Core would see on screen.
- **`weapons/`: the gun's official loadout silhouette**, white with black detail
  on a transparent background (the style the game draws its weapon icons in),
  from the Loadout section of an operator's page, where Ubisoft serves it at
  290 x 100. Trimmed to the gun with 2 px spare, kept at its natural size (so no
  bigger than 290 x 100, well inside 480 x 300) and in its original PNG colour
  mode. The CCE Shield MK2's picture is served as AVIF and was converted to PNG.

Every item has a picture: 78 operators and 117 guns. None is `null`.

