## The loadouts

Each operator item carries `loadout: {primary, secondary}`, the ids of the guns
that operator can pick, and each gun carries `usedBy`, the operators who can
pick it. The two always agree (the build checks both directions).

- **Where they come from: the operator's own page on ubisoft.com** (its Loadout
  section, Primary Weapon and Secondary Weapon), read 2026-09-23. The table
  below gives the page for every operator.
- **Checked against every loadout change Ubisoft published from Year 10 Season
  1 to Y11S3.1** (the list above; also the Y10S1 designer's notes and addendum,
  Y10S1.2, Y10S1.3, Y10S2 designer's notes, Y10S2.0 addendum, Y10S2.3, Y10S3 addendum, Y10S3.1, Y10S3.2, Y10S4.1,
  Y10S4 addendum, Y11S1.1 to Y11S1.3, Y11S2.1 to Y11S2.3, Y11S2.2 designer's
  notes and Y11S3 addendum, none of which moves a gun). The pages carry every change except one: **the
  XK23 is not yet on Rauora's or Sens' page**, though the Y11S2 designer's notes
  add it to both ("Primary weapons: Added XK23") and the System Override page
  says "In addition to Dokkaebi, Rauora and Sens now also have the XK23 as a new
  primary weapon". It is in their loadouts, last, and both are marked uncertain
  for its position.
- **The weapon lists in this season's own notes agree with the pages**: the
  Y11S3 designer's notes (SMG-12: Dokkaebi, Vigil, Warden; SPSMG9: Clash, Kali;
  AR-15.50: Maverick, Tubarão; Mk 14 EBR: Aruni, Dokkaebi) and the Y11S3.1 patch
  notes, dated 2026-09-22 (M1014: Ace, Castle, Pulse, Thermite; SPAS-15:
  Caveira, Thunderbird).
- **Order inside a loadout** is the order the operator's page lists them (for
  Rauora and Sens, with the XK23 after them). Daybreak changed the in-game order
  for most operators and Ubisoft does not say what it is now, so **the page's
  order is not confirmed as the game's**. The newest pages (Dokkaebi, remade for
  System Override, Thatcher's for Tenfold Pursuit, Flores' for Silent Hunt) put
  the newly added gun last.
- **Blackbeard has no secondary weapon.** Since his Year 9 Season 4 remaster his
  H.U.L.L. Adaptable Shield is carried with his primary, and both his page and
  the [Collision Point season page](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/seasons/collisionpoint) list no Secondary Weapon for him. His `secondary` is empty.
- **Shields are primary weapons in Siege**, so Montagne (Le Roc Shield), Blitz
  (G52-Tactical Shield), Clash (CCE Shield MK2) and Fuze (Ballistic Shield) have
  them in `primary`, and they are in the Guns kind as a Shields group. They are
  not guns; the group is there so a shield operator's loadout is complete.

## How the lists are organised, and what is not confirmed

- **Operators** are in two groups, Attackers and Defenders, from the Side on
  each operator's page (the pages also split the roster 39 and 39 under those
  two headings). Inside each: **alphabetical, accents folded** (Capitão with the
  Cs, Jäger with the Js, Nøkk before Nomad). **The in-game operator select
  screen's order was not confirmed** from any official page; Ubisoft's own site
  lists operators newest first, which the game does not.
- **`from` on an operator** is the season they joined, named as Ubisoft's
  [Seasons page](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/seasons) names it ("Year 11 Season 3: Operation Split Fire"; Ubisoft names the seasons from
  Year 6 Season 1 to Year 7 Season 1 without "Operation"). The Seasons page starts at
  Year 1 Season 1, Operation Black Ice; the 20 operators it never introduces
  are the December 2015 launch roster, marked "Launch (2015)". Striker and
  Sentry replaced the Recruit in Year 9 Season 2, Operation New Blood. `from` on
  a gun is `null`.
- **Gun groups are the game's own weapon classes** as Ubisoft defined them in
  the [Year 9 Season 1 designer's notes](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/3jBlCdtRBQx2sCjmY2umNu/y9s1-designers-notes) (Assault Rifle, Submachine Gun, Light Machine Gun, Marksman Rifle,
  Sniper Rifle, Shotgun, Slug Shotgun, Machine Pistol, Handgun, Revolver, Hand
  Cannon: "New classes: Revolver, Sniper Rifle, Slug Shotgun"), plus Shields.
  **The group order is ours** (primary classes, shields, then secondary
  classes), and so is the order inside a group (alphabetical).
- **Class labels.** The operator pages print an older, coarser label under
  each gun; where an official note puts a gun in one of the newer classes, the
  note wins:
  - Revolvers: .44 Vendetta, Keratos .357 and LFP586, named as the Revolvers in
    the [Y9S1.3 designer's notes](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/2D4HsYOBEEg0wEW5dim34o/y9s13-designers-notes) (the pages say Handgun).
  - Slug Shotguns: Glaive-12 (the [Y10S3.3 patch notes](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/4RsdLNZbYZ3wIrcgaDpkuF/y10s33-patch-notes) buff it "to match other slug shotguns")
    and TCSG12 (the Y10S3 designer's notes "add a Slug Shotgun" to Sentry:
    "Added TCSG12"); ACS12 and BOSG.12.2 by inference from the Y9S1 designer's
    notes (marked uncertain).
  - Sniper Rifle: CSRX 300 (marked uncertain; the page says Marksman Rifle).
  - Marksman Rifle: AR-15.50, called a DMR by the [Y11S3 designer's notes](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/PONCuRt8LaCr3O31NkBQb/y11s3-designers-notes) (marked uncertain; the
    pages say Assault Rifle).
  - Blank on the page, class from Ubisoft's text: XK23 Assault Rifle (Y11S2
    designer's notes), PMR90A2 Marksman Rifle (Tenfold Pursuit: "the PMR90A2
    marksman rifle"), Reaper MK2 Machine Pistol (Y10S3 designer's notes: "less
    lethal than other Machine Pistols"), UZK50Gi Submachine Gun (Y10S2
    designer's notes: Submachine Guns, "High caliber (e.g. UZK50GI)"), 9x19VSN
    Submachine Gun (Kapkan's and Tachanka's pages), TACIT .45 and Luison
    Handguns (marked uncertain).
- **Primary or secondary.** The format has no field for it; an operator's
  `loadout` says which. Every class is one or the other except Shotguns (the
  ITA12S and Super Shorty are secondaries) and Slug Shotguns (the Glaive-12 is
  a secondary).

## Names

Operator and gun names are spelt as Ubisoft spells them on the operator pages,
except where those pages set a name in capitals or slip, below. The game draws
names in capitals, so capitalisation never changes what the owner sees on
screen.

| printed | where | the catalog uses | because |
|---|---|---|---|
| NØKK, CAPITÃO | their operator pages and the operator list | Nøkk, Capitão | Ubisoft's running text ("Thatcher, Nøkk, Hibana, and Capitão", Tenfold Pursuit season page) |
| "Azami " (trailing space) | Azami's page | Azami | trimmed |
| 9X19SVN | Azami's page | 9x19VSN | Kapkan's and Tachanka's pages; the real VSN; one gun, one id |
| POF9 | Sens' page, Vector Glare season page | POF-9 | Y9S1.3 and Y11S2 designer's notes and the Y11S1.1 patch notes, which head the gun's own balance entry "POF-9" |
| .44 MAG SEMI-AUTO, .44 VENDETTA | Nomad's, Kaid's and Deimos' pages | .44 Mag Semi-Auto, .44 Vendetta | Y9S1.3 designer's notes |
| LE ROC SHIELD, CCE SHIELD MK2 | Montagne's and Clash's pages | Le Roc Shield, CCE Shield MK2 | Y11S3.1 patch notes ("Montagne's Le Roc Shield"); Clash's by the same rule |
| Commando-9 | Ubisoft News article on Split Fire | Commando 9 | every operator page |
| MK14 EBR, MK 14 EBR | Y11S3 notes | Mk 14 EBR | the operator pages |
| Vector.45 ACP, 556XI, P10 Roni, UZK50GI | designer's notes | Vector .45 ACP, 556xi, P10 RONI, UZK50Gi | the operator pages |

Ids follow `../README.md`. One exception to the slug rule: **Nøkk's id is
`attackers.nokk`**. The letter ø has no accent to drop, so the slug rule turns
it into `n_kk`; `nokk` is Ubisoft's own address for her page and what anyone
would type. `node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js` prints it as a note (an id
that differs from its name's slug), which is expected.

## Uncertain

- `attackers.rauora` (Rauora): Loadout: Ubisoft's operator page does not list the XK23 yet; the Year 11 Season 2 designer's notes added it to this operator's primary weapons, so it is included, placed last because its place in the game's own order is not confirmed.
- `attackers.sens` (Sens): Loadout: Ubisoft's operator page does not list the XK23 yet; the Year 11 Season 2 designer's notes added it to this operator's primary weapons, so it is included, placed last because its place in the game's own order is not confirmed.
- `marksman_rifles.ar_15_50` (AR-15.50): Class: Ubisoft's operator pages label it Assault Rifle, but the Year 11 Season 3 designer's notes call it and the Mk 14 EBR DMRs; filed as a Marksman Rifle.
- `sniper_rifles.csrx_300` (CSRX 300): Class: Ubisoft's operator page labels it Marksman Rifle; Siege has had a Sniper Rifle class since Year 9 Season 1 and Ubisoft calls the CSRX 300 a bolt-action sniper rifle, but no official page names the class's members; filed as a Sniper Rifle.
- `slug_shotguns.acs12` (ACS12): Class: Ubisoft's operator pages label it Shotgun; the Year 9 Season 1 designer's notes give Defenders the Magnified scope only on Slug Shotguns, Marksman Rifles and some SMGs and list the ACS12 among them, so it is filed as a Slug Shotgun.
- `slug_shotguns.bosg_12_2` (BOSG.12.2): Class: Ubisoft's operator pages label it Shotgun; the Year 9 Season 1 designer's notes give Defenders the Magnified scope only on Slug Shotguns, Marksman Rifles and some SMGs and list the BOSG.12.2 among them, so it is filed as a Slug Shotgun.
- `handguns.luison` (Luison): Class: Ubisoft's operator page leaves the class blank; Caveira's suppressed pistol, filed as a Handgun.
- `handguns.tacit_45` (TACIT .45): Class: Ubisoft's operator page leaves the class blank; the Silent Hunt season page calls it a sidearm, so it is filed as a Handgun.

