## Update the list when a season changes it

Siege adds an operator or a gun, or moves guns between operators, most seasons
(early March, June, September, December) and sometimes mid-season.

1. Read the new season's page (from [the Seasons page](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/seasons)) and its designer's notes and patch
   notes on [Ubisoft's news page](https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/game/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates). Look for "LOADOUT", "Primary weapons: Added", "Secondary
   weapons" and new operators.
2. A new operator: add it to its side's group in alphabetical place, id
   `attackers.<slug>` or `defenders.<slug>`, `from` the season's name, its
   `loadout`, and its icon from its operator page (the `r6s-operators-badge-...`
   image) saved as `operators/<slug>.png`, with a row in the Operators pictures
   table.
3. A new gun: add it to its class's group with `usedBy`, and its silhouette
   from the Loadout section of an operator's page, trimmed, saved as
   `weapons/<slug>.png`, with a row in the Guns pictures table.
4. A gun added to or removed from an operator: change both that operator's
   `loadout` and the gun's `usedBy`. They must agree.
5. Ids never change and are never reused (see `../README.md`).
6. Set `asOf` and `season`, then run `node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js`.
